  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N appears to have multiple targets that ultimately lead to CAL-51 through a series of biochemical pathways. The evidence suggests that Mollicellin N interacts with Leukocyte common antigen, which is a target of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, and this compound further targets CAL-51. Similarly, Mollicellin N also interacts with A704, which is a target of the same compound, reinforcing the connection between Mollicellin N and CAL-51. Additionally, Mollicellin N is linked to P2X purinoceptor 1, which is targeted by a different compound that also leads to CAL-51. These findings collectively indicate that Mollicellin N may act through various molecular mechanisms to influence CAL-51, potentially through the activation of different receptors or signaling pathways. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship between Mollicellin N and CAL-51, suggesting that the drug may exert its effects through multiple distinct mechanisms, each contributing to the final outcome.",
